WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:08.070
Jen Grisanti: I think that if there were an
exact science as to what will hit, then writers

00:00:08.070 --> 00:00:09.890
would be making it all over the place.

00:00:09.890 --> 00:00:16.020
I think really, I’m going to tell you from
being a studio executive for the number of

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:24.160
years that I was and still being a writing
instructor at NBC and studying pilots and

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:31.800
knowing that Hollywood doesn’t know exactly
what’s going to hit, they are throwing it

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:40.100
out there and praying that Middle America
is going to show up.

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:48.460
And I think if you were to survey a bunch
of studio executives at the beginning of each

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:55.300
season and say what shows do you think are
going to be the breakout hits versus what

00:00:55.300 --> 00:01:02.160
shows are already, it’s hit or miss.

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:11.979
Like when you take a show like TRANSPARENT,
I’m sure there were so many doubts about

00:01:11.979 --> 00:01:14.119
that show, would it hit?

00:01:14.119 --> 00:01:21.890
Yet we take someone like Jill Soloway who
did SIX FEET UNDER and you know that she has

00:01:21.890 --> 00:01:30.340
a track record and you know it’s based on
emotional truth and you look at the current

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:38.630
climate in the world and everything just happened
together.

00:01:38.630 --> 00:01:40.200
I think that happens a lot.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:47.350
I definitely think there are shows that the
first season blows peoples minds and so therefore

00:01:47.350 --> 00:01:54.509
all the expectation isn’t on the second
season and that is a large expectation.

00:01:54.509 --> 00:02:00.279
Film Courage: So you’ve seen that a lot
where the first season is amazing and for

00:02:00.279 --> 00:02:02.080
some reason the second season falls short.

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:03.080
Jen Grisanti: Yes!

00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:06.119
Film Courage: Is that because the writing
becomes stale or it’s not clear?

00:02:06.119 --> 00:02:15.040
Jen Grisanti: I believe that is because the
series concept wasn’t set up in a strong

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:25.470
enough way to understand what season two,
three and four will be and I’ve seen shows…say

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:26.470
for example LOST.

00:02:26.470 --> 00:02:31.340
LOST was developed oddly enough at Spelling
[Entertainment Group] even though it went

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:37.510
to ABC because the writer…Spelling was going
to do it with ABC but then the writer Spelling

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:43.489
had, the script didn’t come in the way that
ABC wanted it so they got Damon Lindelof and

00:02:43.489 --> 00:02:44.489
J.J.

00:02:44.489 --> 00:02:47.050
Abrams who had overall deals there.

00:02:47.050 --> 00:02:54.860
Now LOST, to my understanding, did not have
a clear sense of what the show was going to

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:59.489
be beyond the first season and it worked.

00:02:59.489 --> 00:03:06.939
And that was okay because the concept was
set up in a strong enough way that we cared

00:03:06.939 --> 00:03:14.569
and we wanted to return and the way it evolved
each season was mind-blowing because we were

00:03:14.569 --> 00:03:17.040
with them.

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:26.030
The set-up of the series arc was strong enough
even though there wasn’t clarity on what

00:03:26.030 --> 00:03:34.250
the other seasons were going to be versus
other shows where you could feel that they

00:03:34.250 --> 00:03:39.879
had one really strong season in them and are
they going to be able to keep up with that?

00:03:39.879 --> 00:03:48.239
And I think the mistake that is made that
leads to the show not succeeding is that season

00:03:48.239 --> 00:03:53.019
two goes too far away from the core concept
that was set up.

00:03:53.019 --> 00:03:53.170
Question for the viewers: What TV show disappointed
you the most in Season 2?

